# 5. Methodology

The assessment followed a reconnaissance-oriented methodology.

## Phase 1: Domain Information Gathering

WHOIS was used to retrieve domain registration information.

## Phase 2: Passive Information Gathering

theHarvester was used with the CRT.sh data source to search for publicly available certificate-related information.

## Phase 3: DNS Enumeration

DNSenum was used to identify DNS records, nameservers, mail servers and associated hostnames.

## Phase 4: Web Technology Fingerprinting

WhatWeb was used to identify the target website's technologies, CMS and web server.

## Phase 5: WAF Identification

WAFW00F was used to identify the likely Web Application Firewall technology.

## Phase 6: Network Reconnaissance

Nmap was used to identify network ports, service states and detected software versions.

## Phase 7: Graphical Network Scanning

Zenmap was used to perform and review a network scan through its graphical interface.

